!Name: deepcell
!CDeep Cell by Jared James Prince.  A slight modification of David
!CBell's Unit Cell, see Unit Cell for background.  Runs 2 Life universes
!Cinstead of 1(referred to as A0 and B0).  The 2 universes do not
!Cinteract.   Period 7680.  The ON/OFF state of A0 is found every 7680
!Crounds and is indicated by the presence/absence of a glider
!Cbetween the 6 boats in the upper left quadrant.  The state of B0 is
!Cindicated the same way but offset by 3840 rounds.  So every  n*7680
!Cfor A0 and n*7680+3840 for B0.  This version is set with A0 initially
!CON (indicated by glider in boats) and B0 in a pre-start ON state
!C(indicated by 3 blocks in the vertical chamber in the lower left
!Cquadrant) so B0 will be officially ON in 3840 rounds.  To start A0 OFF,
!Cdelete the glider.  To start B0 OFF, delete the 3 blocks. An infinite
!Ctiling of Deep Cells allows for an infinite hierarchy as follows:  Set
!Cuniverse A0 to generate an arbitrary Life pattern.  Set universe B0 to
!Cgenererate another layer of Deep Cells.  This new layer has two
!Cuniverses, called A1 and B1.  Set universe A1 to generate an arbitrary
!C Life pattern.  Set universe B1 to generate another layer of Deep
!CCells.  This new layer has two universes, called A2 and B2.  Set
!Cuniverse A2 to generate an arbitrary Life pattern.  Set universe B2 to
!Cgenerate another layer of Deep Cells.  This new layer has two
!Cuniverses, called A3 and B3...
!CWritten in 1998 but couldn't be tested properly, forgotten, then
!Cremembered and tested 2004.  jared@psychoticdeath.com
!Source: jslife-oversize-20100113
